export const academicArticles: AcademicArticle[] = [
  {
    id: "between-carbon-and-code",
    title: "在碳與代碼之間：算法視覺時代的材料抵抗",
    titleEn: "Between Carbon and Code: Wu Xiaodong’s Material Resistance in the Age of Algorithmic Vision",
    author: "Wu Xiaodong Studio Academic Archive / 學術檔案部",
    authorEn: "Wu Xiaodong Studio Academic Archive",
    excerpt: "在數字算法席卷視覺秩序的今天，吳曉東的工作通過逆向引入宣紙、礦物顏料與地球重力的物理阻力，建立了一種『第三條路線』——不是純淨的傳統筆墨秩序，也不是冷漠的硅基計算，而是於兩者之間尋找有機的、有生命力的，能夠自我增殖與變化的藝術語言。",
    excerptEn: "In an era of generic silicon interfaces, Wu's practice reintroduces the visceral resistance of Xuan paper, dry pigments, and gravitational vectors, creating a 'Third Route' that challenges both classical brush tradition and sterile code rendering.",
    content: "在當代視覺文化被算法邏輯與像素平滑性（Pixel Smoothness）迅速同質化的今天，架上繪畫正面臨一種前所未有的本体論危機。當機器生成圖像（AIGC）以一種“無摩擦”的狀態吞噬人類的肉身視覺經驗時，手工痕跡的物質性究竟仍具有何種形而上意義？中國藝術家吳曉東的實踐，恰恰在這一技術與文明的斷裂點上，構建出一種極具學術張力的視覺回應。一、 媒介作為證詞：宣紙的“生物基質”重構與地質時間性。吳曉東的媒介實驗並不試圖回避當下的數字技術時代，也並非簡單地退守傳統水墨的避風港。相反，他通過一種“新物質主義（New Materialism）”的全球學術視角，重新定義了中國傳統宣紙。在他的創作語境中，宣紙不再僅僅是承載圖像的被動平面，而是一個多孔、吸附性強且具有獨特“滲化”效果的活性空間。宣紙纖維的交織形態被他重構為一種“生物基質（Bio-matrix）”，在物理層面上模擬著碳基生物在自然環境中的代謝與呼吸。二、 垂直流變與基因點陣：對沖矽基秩序的生物編碼。在具體的方法論上，吳曉東發展出了兩套高度嚴謹且相輔相成的獨特視覺語言：“垂直流淌線條（Vertical Fluidity）”與“基因式點陣（Genetic Pointillism）”。吳曉東最具辨識度的“垂直流淌線條”，是利用重力干預引導顏料沿宣紙纖維縫隙自然下行。這種語法是對重力場域的精確回應，以及對物理學中“熵（Entropy）”與“能量耗散”的哲學思辨。它以一種不可逆的自然流變量，對沖了AI算法中由0與1構成的、可逆且絕對受控的數字秩序。與流動線條相呼應的是其“基因式點陣”結構。在作品中，這些密集的細胞化群落、類微生物的黑褐色斑點或嵌套孔洞，並非冷峻、理性的西方幾何網格，而是“生物遺傳密碼”的視覺化表征。三、 確立“第三條路線”：後人類語境下的碳基自然主義。吳曉東的學術定位，填補了當代藝術在“後人類主義（Post-humanism）”全球討論中關於東方媒介表達的空白。他的實踐既非對西方冷幾何極簡主義的盲目模仿，亦非對傳統筆墨的簡單當代化翻版，而是在兩者之間開辟了極具先鋒性的“第三條路線”（The Third Route）。他將這種實踐命名為“碳基自然主義”（Carbon-based Naturalism）。",
    contentEn: "In an era of generic silicon interfaces, Wu's practice reintroduces the visceral resistance of Xuan paper, dry pigments, and gravitational vectors, creating a 'Third Route' that challenges both classical brush tradition and sterile code rendering. I. Medium as Witness: Reconstruction of Xuan Paper's 'Bio-matrix' and Tectonic Duration. Wu's medium experimentation does not attempt to evade the digital age, nor does it retreat into the comfort zone of traditional ink. Instead, through a global academic perspective of 'New Materialism', he redefines traditional Chinese Xuan paper. In his creative context, Xuan paper is no longer a passive plane carrying images, but an active space that is porous, highly absorbent, and possesses a unique 'bleeding' effect. The interwoven form of Xuan paper fibers is reconstructed as a 'Bio-matrix', simulating the metabolism and respiration of carbon-based organisms in their natural environment at a physical level. II. Vertical Flux and Genetic Dot-Matrices: Biological Coding Against Silicon Order. Methodologically, Wu has developed two highly rigorous and complementary visual languages: 'Vertical Fluidity' and 'Genetic Pointillism.' His iconic vertical flowing lines are generated by gravitational intervention guiding pigments downward along the fibrous gaps of Xuan paper. This syntax precisely responds to gravitational fields and philosophically contemplates 'Entropy' and 'Energy Dissipation'. With its irreversible natural flux, it counters the reversible and absolutely controlled digital order of 0s and 1s in AI algorithms. Corresponding to the fluid lines are his 'Genetic Dot-Matrices' structures. These dense cellular clusters and microbial-like dark spots are not cold, rational Western geometric grids, but visual representations of 'biological genetic codes.' III. Establishing 'The Third Route': Carbon-Based Naturalism in Post-Humanist Discourse. Wu's academic positioning fills a structural vacancy in the global post-humanist discussion regarding Eastern medium expressions. His practice is neither a blind imitation of Western cold geometry nor a simple contemporization of traditional ink, but opens a pioneering 'Third Route' between the two, which he terms 'Carbon-based Naturalism.'",
    date: "2026.05"
  }
];

